[1879342140]={[1]="Brooch of Bone";[2]="This brooch of bone belonged to a Lossoth man named Oiva, and it was gifted to you by his widow Pinja when you cleansed it of the corruption that had fastened to it in Mordor.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342141]={[1]="Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân";[2]="This sculpture was carved by Bhai-buri-Ghân before he was slain by Orcs, and it was gifted to you by his brother Khôr-buri-Ghân, who was grateful for your help in discovering this unseen side of his brother. It was taken into Mordor, but has returned and been cleansed of the evil that corrupted it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342142]={[1]="Badge of Ariant";[2]="This badge was worn by a guard of High King Elendil at the Bridge of Ariant, in Annúminas. The badge was taken into Mordor, but has returned and been cleansed of the evil that corrupted it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342143]={[1]="Corrupted Sceptre";[2]="This sceptre Is about two feet long and holds an orb at one clawed end, near which faint markings can be seen. Gandalf believes this sceptre is an heirloom of the Kingdom of Cardolan. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342144]={[1]="Corrupted Bone Fragment";[2]="This bone fragment may have splintered from a spear-point such as those used by the tribes of Enedwaith and Dunland. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342145]={[1]="Corrupted Shard";[2]="This small shard has splintered off the tusk of a porcine animal. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342146]={[1]="Vengeance of Folca";[2]="This shard of tusk splintered from the tusk of the Great Boar of Everholt, which slew and was slain by King Folca of Rohan. The Boar-tribe of the Eastfold worshipped the tusk-shard, but it was taken into Mordor against their wishes. It has returned and been cleansed of the evil that corrupted it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342147]={[1]="Corrupted Badge";[2]="This small badge or medal is reminiscent of the type that is sometimes worn by guards at their posts, and Gandalf believes that this one was worn by a guard of High King Elendil at Annúminas. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342148]={[1]="Corrupted Key";[2]="This stone key is very angular and covered in runes that mark it as unlocking a door somewhere in Khazad-dûm. The time it spent in Mordor has added to its corruption, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342149]={[1]="Seeds of Defiance";[2]="These seeds were entrusted to Trotsiv of the Earth-kin, and he protected them from those who would do them harm. Though the pouch was brought into Mordor, and corruption ensnared it, the seeds within could not be ruined or destroyed, and now you have cleansed it of that evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342150]={[1]="Key of the Forgotten";[2]="This key was used to seal away an archive in Khazad-dûm, but the holder of the key was slain and the key he bore was taken into Mordor. Forgotten, the dwarves that were sealed away survived as long as they could, but came in time to a sad end. You unlocked the door, and in so doing cleansed the key's corruption.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342151]={[1]="Corrupted Sculpture";[2]="This small sculpture of a woman is carved from bone or tusk. One hand is raised as if in warning, and in the other she holds a spear ready to throw at an unseen foe. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342152]={[1]="Image of the Champion";[2]="This sculpture was carved by Bemwin, a skilled artist who loved the champion Darothild and made this representation of her shortly before she faced the Red-maid, and perished. It was taken into Mordor, but has returned and been cleansed of the evil that corrupted it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342153]={[1]="Corrupted Pouch";[2]="This leather bag is sealed with a strap of cord tied in a simple-looking knot, but the knot resists any attempt to untie it. The time the pouch spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342154]={[1]="Sceptre of Cardolan";[2]="This sceptre belonged to a forgotten prince of Cardolan, who stood against the men of Carn Dûm but was slain. The sceptre was taken into Mordor, but has returned and been cleansed of the evil that corrupted it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342155]={[1]="Corrupted Brooch";[2]="This brooch is made of bone and encircled by a curved piece of what appears to be antler. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342156]={[1]="Corrupted Cup";[2]="This cup is fashioned of clay used by the hill-men of Rhudaur during the days of their ascendancy, and it has a single blood-red ruby mounted on one side. The time it spent in Mordor has added to its corruption, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342157]={[1]="Needle of Many Leagues";[2]="This needle of the Uch-lûth travelled many leagues within the body of the Orc that slew Deilur more than fifty years ago, before it finally meted her justice upon him. The corruption that affixed to the needle in Mordor has been cleansed by returning it to the land that Deilur called home.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342158]={[1]="Cup of Sacrifice";[2]="This cup was used by Rhudauran priests in their vile ceremonies, but it has been cleansed of its evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342161]={[1]="Corrupted Figurine";[2]="This small sculpture is carved in the shape of a squat, humanoid figure, reminiscent of the Púkel-men that guard the road to Dunharrow. The time it spent in Mordor has corrupted it, and now it radiates a feeling of great evil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342185]={[1]="Bubbling Water";[2]="Water cascades in a frigid rush, down from the heights of the Misty Mountains.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342186]={[1]="Locked Door";[2]="Many are the mysteries that remain locked away behind doors in Khazad-dûm, and even dwarves cannot say what might lie behind them.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879342187]={[1]="Locked Door";[2]="Many are the mysteries that remain locked away behind doors in Khazad-dûm, and even dwarves cannot say what might lie behind them.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
