[1879358682]={[1]="Ash-worn Page";[2]="But on the day the Mountain was rent asunder and its fires cascaded, when the iron walls of Naerband became not just a prison, but an oven.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358683]={[1]="Ash-worn Page";[2]="When the screams of the roasting doomed filled the air, I beheld that savage masterwork and knew that Sauron, even in death and ruin, was truly the master.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358685]={[1]="Ash-worn Page";[2]="By His command, I devised pains and torments unequalled in any of the Ages of the world.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358686]={[1]="Lost Lore: Naerband Prison";[2]="A record of the lost lore of Naerband.";[3]=85;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358687]={[1]="Ash-worn Page";[2]="Before the Mountain raged, I was the master of all that transpired within the iron walls of the Direhold. I was the greatest of the Dark Lord's torturers.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358688]={[1]="Ash-worn Page";[2]="I have much to learn if I am to become Shakh Thraknûl, and surpass the Dark Lord in the arts of pain. I need some new captives.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358689]={[1]="Ash-worn Page";[2]="Before the Mountain raged, I was called Thraknûl. I was the warden of Naerband, the greatest of Lord Sauron's prisons.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358768]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="Seven years...a mere seven years, and I heard the truth in Sauron's words. Gil-galad had left me to die, and Sauron in His kindness wrought for me a new form and granted me a place among His greatest servants. Seven years, and He was defeated...but He will return.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358769]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="Long after Sauron's fall, the Lord of the Nazgûl decreed that it was His will to gather the Seven Rings to Mordor. Sindya and Taurya had been wrested from the unworthy fingers of Dwarf-kings in the East, but none in Mordor -- not even the Nazgûl -- dared to seek the Ring of Durin, Angya.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358770]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="As Sauron had willed it, the Rings could not be unmade by dragon-fire. Thostír and Hrímil were soon subdued, and the Weeping Warrior dragged them beyond the Lithannon into the deepest dungeons of the Mordath. Thus, Tínya and Tulcya were returned to Mordor.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358771]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="Four of the Seven remained lost and hidden in the Dwarf-kingdoms of Middle-earth, and so it was that the Lord of the Nazgûl ordered one of the Gúrzyul, the Weeping Warrior, to find them.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358772]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="With the Ring-drakes imprisoned, only Úrya and Vanya remained lost. The Lord of the Nazgûl soon revealed that a great Worm had survived the breaking of Thangorodrim. Desperate to escape the wrath of the Elves in the Elder Days, the Worm had sought shelter in the depths of the Ered Luin.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358773]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="To the East, the Nazgûl had spied the Dwarf-kingdoms in possession of the Rings Tínya and Tulcya left in ruin, but they ventured no nearer for they sensed an ancient, terrible power lurking within each of the dwarves' broken halls.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358774]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="Long had the great Worm remained hidden in the Ered Luin, indeed long enough to be forgotten, but as the hoards of those wielding Úrya and Vanya grew, so too did his greed. Heedless of all peril, the Worm sacked the Dwarf-kingdoms and devoured the last of the Seven.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358775]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="Indeed, it was Dragons that had laid claim to Tínya and Tulcya. A fire-drake, Thostír the Rank, and a cold-drake, Hrímil Frost-heart, had destroyed the Dwarf-kingdoms of the eastern mountains, and knowingly or not, they swallowed the Rings of Power as well as the Dwarf-kings who wielded them.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358776]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="And so, the Lord of the Nazgûl granted the Weeping Warrior the Dwarf-ring, Sindya, to draw the Worm from the Ered Luin. Powerless to resist his greed, the great Worm followed the Weeping Warrior into the East. When at last the Worm tired in his pursuit, he fell broken before the Ephel Dúath.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879358777]={[1]="Forgotten Page";[2]="Thus, the great Worm was cast into Glurnákh, the Pit of Greed. For countless years, the Weeping Warrior brought his greatest tortures upon each of the Ring-drakes, but none yielded the Rings. Neither death nor mercy shall be granted to them, not before they surrender the Rings of Power.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
