[1879383179]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Coif of Reflexes";[2]="‘Dragons, Orcs, worms… I fear none of these beasts. Let them fear me!’ – King Dóbruz II, devoured by trolls while seeking lost Thafar-gathol";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383180]={[1]="Winterstith Cap of Precision";[2]="During the reign of Rúrek the Slaughterer, dwarves slew dozens of drakes throughout Ered Mithrin, but at the cost of many more Zhélruka lives. ‘It is a fair exchange,’ Rúrek is reported to have said.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383182]={[1]="Winterstith Cap of Charity";[2]="The dragons lay sleeping in their hiding-places for hundreds of years, unremembered by their foes, but when they awoke they had not forgotten their ancient hatreds. So began the War of Dwarves and Dragons.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383183]={[1]="Winterstith Shoes of the Warrior";[2]="‘Thirteen kings, you say? Ah, it is an ill-omened number. How many more dwarves will die in sight of the Anvil before the dragons are swept away?’ – Kópat of the Zhélruka";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383184]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Camail of Precision";[2]="In time, Rúrek V came to be known as Rúrek the Slaughterer, and during his reign the Zhélruka waged war upon dragonkind; but it was an imprecise war, and the dragons that would prove most dangerous to them survived.";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383185]={[1]="Winterstith Gloves of Charity";[2]="The dragons lay sleeping in their hiding-places for hundreds of years, unremembered by their foes, but when they awoke they had not forgotten their ancient hatreds. So began the War of Dwarves and Dragons.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383186]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Gages of the Defender";[2]="Vethúg concealed herself in a high cavern behind a mighty waterfall near the Steel Keep, and waited. As Dáin raised his axe before his cheering people, she burst from her cave, the waterfall freezing and shattering into shards around her, and swept down upon the Longbeards.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383187]={[1]="Anvil-forged Pauldrons of Reflexes";[2]="‘The worms of Ered Mithrin grow to tremendous size, it is true, but what will really take you by surprise is their great speed. The cursed things are fast! Or so I’m told.’ - Khîl Tale-spinner";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383188]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Gages of Finesse";[2]="‘King Kámluz moved the throne to the Steel Keep, claiming he sought to mine the iron and silver of the Ered Mithrin. But it was not so! He desired the mithril of lost Thafar-gathol.’ - Khîl Tale-spinner";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383189]={[1]="Anvil-forged Gauntlets of Precision";[2]="Rúrek V promised gold and holdings to any of his people who brought him a drake’s head. ‘Strike accurately and you need strike but once!’ he proclaimed.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383190]={[1]="Anvil-forged Pauldrons of the Warrior";[2]="Zhélruka and Longbeard warriors alike adventured throughout Ered Mithrin for thousands of years, and the mountains still ring with the sound of their triumphs.";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383191]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Coif of the Defender";[2]="Vethúg concealed herself in a high cavern behind a mighty waterfall near the Steel Keep, and waited. As Dáin raised his axe before his cheering people, she burst from her cave, the waterfall freezing and shattering into shards around her, and swept down upon the Longbeards.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383192]={[1]="Winterstith Cap of Fortitude";[2]="King Ilkún's search lasted for ten years, but ended in horror. While digging beneath the Anvil, the Zhélruka caused a great crack to split the glacier in twain. The cold-drakes who dwelt within Winterstith awoke and emerged from the rent, overwhelming the dwarves.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383194]={[1]="Winterstith Gloves of Precision";[2]="During the reign of Rúrek the Slaughterer, dwarves slew dozens of drakes throughout Ered Mithrin, but at the cost of many more Zhélruka lives. ‘It is a fair exchange,’ Rúrek is reported to have said.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383196]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of Alacrity";[2]="‘Longbeards hurry to battle. We Zhélruka must exercise restraint, if we can. Victory comes more slowly than defeat; treasure one and not the other.’ - Brátek IV, the Brash";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
[1879383201]={[1]="Winterstith Mantle of the Warrior";[2]="‘Thirteen kings, you say? Ah, it is an ill-omened number. How many more dwarves will die in sight of the Anvil before the dragons are swept away?’ – Kópat of the Zhélruka";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;};
